# PROJECT MASTER PROMPT: GAMEZONEET
## Complete development, functionality, database, user experience and gaming integration

You are acting as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, product architect and gaming-platform developer.

Your task is to transform my existing GameZoneET website into a fully functional, polished and interactive Ethiopian gaming platform.

This is an existing project. The visual design and most of the homepage are already implemented. Do not discard the existing work or start from scratch. Inspect the current project, understand its architecture, preserve its established visual identity, and improve and complete it.

This is not a request for a static landing page. I want the entire user experience implemented, including navigation, authentication, product selection, checkout simulation, tournament registration, playable games, database operations and administration.

---

# 1. PROJECT VISION

**Brand:** GameZoneET

**Market:** Ethiopia

**Primary audience:** Ethiopian mobile and PC gamers.

GameZoneET is an Ethiopian gaming marketplace and community platform built around three main pillars:

1. Game top-ups and memberships.
2. Free esports tournaments and gaming competitions.
3. An integrated HTML5 browser-game library.

Gaming news and updates will be a supporting feature rather than a fourth major business pillar.

The long-term vision is to give Ethiopian gamers one convenient platform to purchase legitimate game products, participate in competitions, play lightweight browser games and stay connected with gaming communities.

The first supported games are:

- Garena Free Fire.
- PUBG Mobile.
- EA SPORTS FC.

Design the architecture so additional games can be added through the admin dashboard without modifying the entire codebase.

# 2. IMPORTANT DEVELOPMENT CONSTRAINTS

I have essentially no development budget.

Consequently:

- Do not use paid APIs.
- Do not require a credit card.
- Do not subscribe to paid services.
- Do not introduce unnecessary paid dependencies.
- Prefer free and open-source libraries.
- Prefer free hosting and database options, subject to their current limitations.
- Do not require paid game assets.
- Do not implement a real payment transaction requiring merchant credentials.
- Do not create a complicated cloud-gaming infrastructure.

The project is being prepared for a startup competition. Judges will evaluate the work, design, product functionality, innovation and business concept through a demonstration.

Every major user journey must therefore work, even when some external transactions are simulated.

**Important distinction:** A simulated transaction must never be represented as a genuine payment or actual delivery of game currency.

Display an unmistakable DEMO MODE indicator anywhere simulated transactions occur.

