# 7. PILLAR THREE: INTEGRATED HTML5 GAME LIBRARY

This is an important differentiator.

The main goal is to allow Ethiopian gamers to play lightweight games directly through GameZoneET.

Our users may have older laptops and limited computing resources.

We are not building a cloud-gaming service.

Do not implement GTA streaming, remote GPUs or complicated multiplayer servers.

Instead, build a lightweight HTML5 game library.

## Technical approach

Prioritize:

- HTML5 Canvas.
- JavaScript browser games.
- Phaser.
- Lightweight WebGL games only when necessary.

Games should work inside GameZoneET through:

1. Self-hosted game files.
2. Properly licensed game embeds.
3. Official iframe integrations explicitly permitted by the developer.

Never scrape or copy copyrighted games from unrelated websites.

Do not bypass X-Frame-Options, Content Security Policy or other anti-embedding restrictions.

Do not use third-party game URLs in iframes unless embedding is explicitly permitted.

A link working in a normal browser does not mean it is legally or technically embeddable.

Prefer self-hosting legally reusable games when the license allows it.

